WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.234
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.979
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:16.505
Unit eighteen: Human Rights Advocacy. Today you will add information with non-defining relative clauses.

4
00:00:16.805 --> 00:00:19.353
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.498
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:25.537
Human rights.

7
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:29.664
Human rights means basic rights every person has.

8
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.250
Education is a human right.

9
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.665
Your turn. Say: Human rights.

10
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.861
Human rights.

11
00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:41.769
Advocacy.

12
00:00:42.783 --> 00:00:45.897
Advocacy means speaking up to support a cause.

13
00:00:46.483 --> 00:00:48.611
Her advocacy helped refugees.

14
00:00:49.217 --> 00:00:51.985
Your turn. Say: Advocacy.

15
00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:56.171
Advocacy.

16
00:00:56.917 --> 00:00:58.045
Justice.

17
00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.468
Justice means fair treatment for everyone.

18
00:01:02.083 --> 00:01:04.013
People marched for justice.

19
00:01:04.617 --> 00:01:07.118
Your turn. Say: Justice.

20
00:01:09.967 --> 00:01:11.130
Justice.

21
00:01:11.883 --> 00:01:12.966
Equality.

22
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:16.414
Equality means the same rights for all.

23
00:01:17.017 --> 00:01:19.957
Equality means equal pay for equal work.

24
00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:23.168
Your turn. Say: Equality.

25
00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:27.127
Equality.

26
00:01:27.883 --> 00:01:28.908
Activist.

27
00:01:29.917 --> 00:01:32.868
Activist means a person who works for change.

28
00:01:33.483 --> 00:01:35.611
The young activist spoke at the UN.

29
00:01:36.217 --> 00:01:38.799
Your turn. Say: Activist.

30
00:01:41.633 --> 00:01:42.588
Activist.

31
00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:44.850
Awareness campaign.

32
00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:49.754
Awareness campaign means an effort to teach people about an issue.

33
00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:53.406
We started an awareness campaign about child labour.

34
00:01:54.017 --> 00:01:57.342
Your turn. Say: Awareness campaign.

35
00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:01.735
Awareness campaign.

36
00:02:02.483 --> 00:02:03.647
Legislation.

37
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.184
Legislation means laws made by a government.

38
00:02:07.783 --> 00:02:10.131
New legislation protects workers.

39
00:02:10.717 --> 00:02:13.439
Your turn. Say: Legislation.

40
00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.522
Legislation.

41
00:02:18.283 --> 00:02:19.308
Dignity.

42
00:02:20.317 --> 00:02:23.489
Dignity means the respect every person deserves.

43
00:02:24.083 --> 00:02:25.955
Everyone deserves dignity.

44
00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:29.028
Your turn. Say: Dignity.

45
00:02:31.867 --> 00:02:32.659
Dignity.

46
00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:37.048
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:37.883 --> 00:02:40.939
Visal, who fights for human rights?

48
00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:46.023
Activists, who often risk a lot, fight for justice.

49
00:02:47.117 --> 00:02:48.234
Can you name one?

50
00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:54.554
Malala, who was attacked for going to school, now speaks for girls everywhere.

51
00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:56.779
What has changed?

52
00:02:57.883 --> 00:03:04.376
New legislation, which protects girls' education, was passed in many countries.

53
00:03:05.533 --> 00:03:07.359
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:08.217 --> 00:03:11.284
Grammar focus: Advanced relative clauses.

55
00:03:11.584 --> 00:03:12.783
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:13.483 --> 00:03:17.433
Activists, who often risk a lot, fight for justice.

57
00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:21.824
Malala, who was attacked for going to school, speaks for girls.

58
00:03:22.717 --> 00:03:25.831
The law, which was passed last year, protects workers.

59
00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:34.414
Non-defining relative clauses add extra information between commas. Use 'who' for people and 'which' for things. Don't use 'that' here.

60
00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:39.764
Be careful! Don't say: Activists, which risk a lot, fight for justice.

61
00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:45.441
Say: Activists, who risk a lot, fight for justice.

62
00:03:45.741 --> 00:03:47.160
Use 'who' for people.

63
00:03:47.967 --> 00:03:50.851
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:53.039
Voices for Rights.

65
00:03:53.339 --> 00:03:55.501
Human rights belong to every person.

66
00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.916
Activists, who often risk a lot, fight for justice.

67
00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:05.837
Awareness campaigns, which reach millions online, teach people about equality.

68
00:04:06.833 --> 00:04:09.924
New legislation can protect dignity and rights.

69
00:04:10.933 --> 00:04:13.688
Advocacy starts when one person speaks up.

70
00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:19.452
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:20.317 --> 00:04:23.663
Activists, blank risk a lot, fight for justice.

72
00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.618
A, who. B, which. C, what.

73
00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:31.841
The answer is A: who.

74
00:04:32.983 --> 00:04:34.936
Laws made by a government are blank.

75
00:04:35.236 --> 00:04:39.459
A, legislation. B, advocacy. C, justice.

76
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.267
The answer is A: legislation.

77
00:04:46.417 --> 00:04:49.101
The respect every person deserves is blank.

78
00:04:49.401 --> 00:04:53.031
A, dignity. B, equality. C, activism.

79
00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:58.473
The answer is A: dignity.

80
00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:03.155
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:05:04.017 --> 00:05:06.806
What human rights issue would you like to advocate for?

82
00:05:15.617 --> 00:05:17.047
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:17.347 --> 00:05:27.964
I would like to advocate for children's education. Many children, who live in poor villages, cannot go to school, and I want that to change.

84
00:05:28.264 --> 00:05:30.113
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:31.017 --> 00:05:35.422
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and advanced relative clauses.

86
00:05:35.722 --> 00:05:39.698
Today's value is justice. Stand up for what is fair for everyone.

87
00:05:39.998 --> 00:05:42.592
See you in Unit nineteen. Goodbye!

88
00:05:42.892 --> 00:05:46.462
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

